Here is the commit message:
util: fix condition_free_list_type()

This fixes a bug introduced by c4f58deab56282cd438922203287cb073b861513.

Closes oss-fuzz#13878, oss-fuzz#13882, oss-fuzz#13884, oss-fuzz#13886, and
oss-fuzz#13888.

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by incorrect handling of the linked list of conditions in the `condition_free_list_type` function. Specifically, the function was not properly removing conditions from the list when they matched the specified type, leading to potential memory leaks and incorrect list state management. The original implementation used an outdated parameter name and failed to update the list correctly during iteration.

Here is the patch:

-Condition* condition_free_list_type(Condition *first, ConditionType type) {
-        Condition *c, *n, *r = NULL;
+Condition* condition_free_list_type(Condition *head, ConditionType type) {
+        Condition *c, *n;

-        LIST_FOREACH_SAFE(conditions, c, n, first)
-                if (type < 0 || c->type == type)
+        LIST_FOREACH_SAFE(conditions, c, n, head)
+                if (type < 0 || c->type == type) {
+                        LIST_REMOVE(conditions, head, c);
                         condition_free(c);
-                else if (!r)
-                        r = c;
+                }

-        assert(type >= 0 || !r);
-        return r;
+        assert(type >= 0 || !head);
+        return head;
 }



